05:22:36.100 --> 05:22:38.300
So what is
this euclidean distance?

05:22:38.300 --> 05:22:41.397
Well, this euclidean distance
is defined as the square root

05:22:41.397 --> 05:22:43.800
of the sum of difference
between a new point x

05:22:43.800 --> 05:22:45.500
and an existing Point why

05:22:45.600 --> 05:22:48.984
so for example here we
have Point P1 and P2 Point

05:22:48.984 --> 05:22:51.100
P. 1 is 1 1 and point B 2 is 5

05:22:51.100 --> 05:22:54.800
for so what is the euclidean
distance between both of them?

05:22:55.100 --> 05:22:57.255
So you can say
that euclidean distance is

05:22:57.255 --> 05:22:59.200
a direct distance
between two points.

05:22:59.200 --> 05:23:02.200
So what is the distance
between the point P1 and P2?

05:23:02.300 --> 05:23:05.593
So we Calculate it as
5 minus 1 whole square

05:23:05.593 --> 05:23:07.600
plus 4 minus 1 whole square

05:23:07.600 --> 05:23:11.100
and we can route it
over which results to 5.

05:23:11.430 --> 05:23:13.969
So next is
the Manhattan distance.

05:23:14.500 --> 05:23:17.600
Well, this Manhattan distance is
used to calculate the distance

05:23:17.600 --> 05:23:18.871
between real Vector using

05:23:18.871 --> 05:23:21.471
the sum of their absolute
difference in this case.

05:23:21.471 --> 05:23:23.700
The Manhattan distance
between the point P1

05:23:23.700 --> 05:23:27.900
and P2 is mod of 5 minus 1
plus mod value of 4 minus 1,

05:23:27.900 --> 05:23:29.900
which results to 3 plus 4.

05:23:30.000 --> 05:23:31.200
That is 7.

05:23:31.800 --> 05:23:34.400
So this slide shows
the difference between euclidean

05:23:34.400 --> 05:23:36.833
and Manhattan distance
from point A to point B.

05:23:36.833 --> 05:23:39.202
So euclidean distance is
nothing but the direct

05:23:39.202 --> 05:23:41.663
or the least possible distance
between A and B.

05:23:41.663 --> 05:23:44.500
Whereas the Manhattan distance
is a distance between A

05:23:44.500 --> 05:23:47.300
and B measured along the axis
at right angle.

