and understand what exactly
is unsupervised learning.

06:13:34.600 --> 06:13:38.100
So sometimes the given data
is unstructured and unlabeled

06:13:38.100 --> 06:13:40.370
so it becomes difficult
to classify the data

06:13:40.370 --> 06:13:41.900
into different categories.

06:13:41.900 --> 06:13:45.040
So unsupervised learning
helps to solve this problem.

06:13:45.040 --> 06:13:47.818
This learning is used
to Cluster the input data

06:13:47.818 --> 06:13:51.200
and classes on the basis
of their statistical properties.

06:13:51.200 --> 06:13:52.500
So example, we can cluster

06:13:52.500 --> 06:13:55.500
Different Bikes based
upon the speed limit there.

06:13:55.500 --> 06:13:57.400
Acceleration or the average

06:13:57.400 --> 06:13:58.700
that they are giving so

06:13:58.700 --> 06:14:02.000
and suppose learning is a type
of machine learning algorithm

06:14:02.100 --> 06:14:04.000
used to draw inferences

06:14:04.000 --> 06:14:06.933
from beta sets consisting
of input data

06:14:06.933 --> 06:14:08.933
without labeled responses.

06:14:09.000 --> 06:14:11.111
So if you have a look
at the workflow

06:14:11.111 --> 06:14:13.700
or the process flow
of unsupervised learning,

06:14:13.900 --> 06:14:16.300
so the training data is
collection of information

06:14:16.300 --> 06:14:17.400
without any label.

06:14:17.400 --> 06:14:19.576
We have the machine
learning algorithm

06:14:19.576 --> 06:14:21.599
and then we have
the clustering malls.

06:14:21.599 --> 06:14:22.663
So what it does is

06:14:22.663 --> 06:14:25.500
that distributes the data
into a different class.

06:14:25.800 --> 06:14:28.250
And again, if you provide
any unreliable new data,

06:14:28.250 --> 06:14:29.525
it will make a prediction

06:14:29.525 --> 06:14:32.102
and find out to which cluster
that particular data

06:14:32.102 --> 06:14:33.376
or the data set belongs

06:14:33.376 --> 06:14:36.064
to or the particular data point
belongs to so one

06:14:36.064 --> 06:14:37.300
of the most important

