of similar data points.

06:14:49.900 --> 06:14:52.000
It means grouping
of objects based

06:14:52.000 --> 06:14:55.433
on the information found in
the data describing the object.

06:14:55.433 --> 06:14:57.200
Objects or their relationships

06:14:57.200 --> 06:14:59.473
so clustering malls focus on

06:14:59.473 --> 06:15:02.190
and defying groups
of similar records

06:15:02.190 --> 06:15:03.700
and labeling records

06:15:03.700 --> 06:15:07.187
according to the group to which
they belong now this is done

06:15:07.187 --> 06:15:09.329
without the benefit
of prior knowledge

06:15:09.329 --> 06:15:12.000
about the groups
and their characteristics.

06:15:12.000 --> 06:15:13.016
So and in fact,

06:15:13.016 --> 06:15:16.200
we may not even know exactly
how many groups are

06:15:16.200 --> 06:15:17.100
there to look for.

06:15:17.400 --> 06:15:17.605
Now.

06:15:17.605 --> 06:15:19.723
These models are often
referred to as

06:15:19.723 --> 06:15:21.500
unsupervised learning models,

06:15:21.500 --> 06:15:25.100
since there's no external
standard by which to judge.

06:15:25.100 --> 06:15:26.800
One is
classification performance.

06:15:26.800 --> 06:15:30.095
There are no right or wrong
answers to these model.

